@startuml release_note_flow
' Flow: a release note from the pull request to the users' OdooBot chats.
' Preview: Alt+D (PlantUML extension)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

title Release note - from pull request to users

|Developer|
start
:Write notes/<key>.html in the holder module
<prefix>_release_notes, in the pull request of the change
(front matter: key, title, summary, tags, models;
HTML body with /odoo/action-<module>.<xml_id> buttons);

|Deploy|
:Merge, then -u <prefix>_release_notes;
:the holder's data file calls
_load_release_notes("<prefix>_release_notes"),
which reads the holder's notes/*.html;
if (key already in Odoo?) then (yes)
  :skip the file
(the note is never overwritten);
else (no)
  :create release.note
is_published = False
(visible to managers only);
endif
:Deployed by is set
= the user who ran the deploy;

|Deployer|
:open Release Notes > Unpublished,
read the note, press each button,
check Models;
:press Publish;
if (current user = Deployed by
and at least one model?) then (yes)
  :is_published, Published by,
Published date set;
  if (is_notified?) then (no)
    |OdooBot|
    :direct chat to each active internal user
who can read one of the note's models
(no email);
    :is_notified = True (sent once);
  else (yes)
    :nothing is sent again;
  endif
else (no)
  |Deployer|
  :UserError, nothing published;
endif

|Users|
:read the chat, open the note,
filter / group Release Notes by tag;
stop
@enduml
